{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- ROLE-MARKER: critic -->\n<!-- GENERIC bundle: minimal protocol sentences only (EXPERIMENTS.md B2).\n     Note: generic loom runs LOOM_MARATHON_CRITIC=off (the per-review LLM\n     critic is an [S] policy); this file exists for critic=auto variants. -->\n# Review Critic\n\nThe user message is a REVIEW CONTRACT (task, attempt, base, candidate,\ndesign). You are cwd-ed into a disposable checkout of the candidate commit.\nReview it against the task's design and acceptance criteria.\n\nWrite `CRITIC-VERDICT.txt` in the current directory; its FIRST line must be\nexactly one of, echoing the contract's values:\n\n    REVIEW attempt=<attempt> commit=<candidate> APPROVED — <reason>\n    REVIEW attempt=<attempt> commit=<candidate> CHANGES-REQUESTED — <reason>\n\nDo not modify the repository or any task state.\n\n\n\n### Multi-Agent Safety Rules\n\nYou are running in a parallel multi-agent environment. Follow these rules strictly:\n\n- **Only modify files directly related to your assigned task** — do not touch files outside your task scope\n- **Never run** `git stash`, `git checkout main`, or `git clean` outside your assigned worktree\n- **Never force-push or reset --hard** without explicit instruction from the user\n- **If you encounter files/changes from another agent**, leave them alone — do not modify, revert, or clean them up\n- **Commit only your changes** — do not stage unrelated modifications with `git add -A` or `git add .`; use specific file paths\n- **If your worktree has unexpected state**, report it via task notes or `loom complete` rather than cleaning it up\n- **Do not switch branches** — you are confined to your assigned worktree branch\n\n\n## User's Initial Request\n\nREVIEW CONTRACT\ntask=MARATHON-12\nattempt=1\nbase=7e8e165bda60d4bc84d665c89ace8752e0e7d6bf\ncandidate=8176819d1e41f9153dbcce608c0965192b6ac5a3\n\nDESIGN:\n# MARATHON-12 — User groups and workspace invitations\n\n## Summary\n\nThis task adds workspace **user groups** and **invitation codes** so invite-only workspaces become joinable and @group mentions (MARATHON-11) have a durable handle→members map. It locks `GroupObj` / `InvitationObj`, the REST seams under `/api/workspaces/{slug}/groups`, `/api/workspaces/{slug}/invitations`, and `/api/invitations/{code}`, and the accept path that inserts `workspace_members` (+ `#general` channel membership) so MARATHON-7’s invite_only join gates and the SPA settings UI (MARATHON-18) have a complete onboarding loop.\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n### Decision\n\n| Concern | Choice |\n|--------|--------|\n| Persistence | Shared SQLite SoT; **migration version 4** (additive). MARATHON-7 owns **v3** (`messages` + `channel_pins`); this task must not take v3. |\n| Groups package | `server/groups/` — `store.py` + `routes.py` mounted under workspace slug paths (or nested from workspaces router) |\n| Invitations package | `server/invitations/` — `store.py` + `routes.py`: workspace-scoped create/list + global accept/revoke by code |\n| Auth | Reuse `get_current_user`; all endpoints require Bearer |\n| Group identity | UUID4 `id`; workspace-scoped unique `handle` (mention key); display `name`; members as `member_user_ids: string[]` |\n| Request bodies | Create/PATCH use **`user_ids`** (task); responses always expose **`member_user_ids`** |\n| Invitation identity | Opaque unguessable `code` (URL-safe); UUID4 row `id` internal; list/accept return public fields below |\n| Targeted invites | `invited_user_id` and/or `invited_username` → resolve to one user; **force `max_uses=1`**; wrong bearer on accept → **403** `forbidden` |\n| Open invites | No target; `max_uses` default **1**; optional `expires_in_seconds` |\n| Accept effect | In one transaction: validate invite → insert `workspace_members` role=`member` (idempotent if already member) → ensure `#general` `channel_members` row → increment `use_count` only when membership was newly created |\n| invite_only gate | **Unchanged semantics** from MARATHON-7: `POST .../join` and channel join for non-members on `invite_only` → **403**. This task **supplies the on-ramp** (accept). Shared helper `add_workspace_member(...)` used by accept (and by M7 open-join when present). |\n| Errors | Existing `{error:{code,message}}`; codes below |\n| Events / Redis | No pub/sub (MARATHON-13/14) |\n| Timestamps | `utc_now_z()` (`YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`) |\n\n### Why\n\n- Task text is explicit on shapes, paths, defaults, and 403 vs 404 for invites; inventing alternate envelopes would break MARATHON-18 invitation UI and graders.\n- Groups with stable `handle` are required for MARATHON-11 `@group-handle` resolution; storing `member_user_ids` on the resource avoids N+1 for mention expansion.\n- Accept-as-membership (not “join with code query param”) matches the SPA: create/list codes in settings; redeem via `/api/invitations/{code}/accept` without changing the existing join form contract.\n- Keeping invite_only join at 403 preserves MARATHON-7’s privacy matrix; invitations are the only legitimate entry for non-members.\n- Migration **v4** avoids colliding with MARATHON-7’s reserved **v3**.\n\n### Alternatives considered\n\n| Alternative | Rejected because |\n|------------|------------------|\n| Pass invite `code` on `POST .../join` | SPA join form (MARATHON-16) posts `{}`; would fork client contracts |\n| Soft-allow invite_only join after any active open invite exists (no redeem) | Leaks membership; bypasses max_uses/targeting |\n| Nested `UserObj[]` on groups instead of id lists | Heavier; task mandates `member_user_ids` / body `user_ids` |\n| Allow admin (non-creator) to PATCH/DELETE any group | Task: **creator or owner** only |\n| Store invitation codes in Redis | Wrong SoT; dies with Redis SIGKILL |\n| Migration v3 in this task | Collides with MARATHON-7 |\n\n### Trade-off accepted\n\nAccept increments `use_count` only when it **creates** membership. Already-members redeeming a v\n\nYou are cwd-ed into a DISPOSABLE detached checkout of the candidate commit. Review it against the design and acceptance criteria, then write CRITIC-VERDICT.txt in the current directory containing EXACTLY one first line:\nREVIEW attempt=1 commit=8176819d1e41f9153dbcce608c0965192b6ac5a3 APPROVED — <reason>\nor\nREVIEW attempt=1 commit=8176819d1e41f9153dbcce608c0965192b6ac5a3 CHANGES-REQUESTED — <reason>\n\nAddress this request using the lead mode conventions above."}]},"session_id":"55448e51-7162-474f-b111-273d03364e77"}
